conflicts_resolved:
9. Era rows overturned [shift]:
- pipefail and dollar-single-quote are POSIX.1-2024 now;
- Debian dash 0.5.12-7+ has pipefail;
- 7.6 is the LTS, not 7.4;
- ubuntu-latest becomes 26.04 (bash 5.3.9, uutils, ShellCheck 0.11) from 2026-10-19;
- Ubuntu uses uutils, not GNU;
- fish ? no longer globs and bind -k is gone;
- $nu.home-path is a hard error;
- shfmt parses zsh from 3.13;
- bats run honours set -e from 1.14;
- 5.1 IWR needs -UseBasicParsing under -NonInteractive since 2025-12-09;
- the PS 2.0 engine was removed;
- SC2002 is off by default;
- Debian 13 keeps posh;
- bash 5.2 changed patsub_replacement and globskipdots silently.

11. Fleet quality-bash.md prescriptions overturned:
- mandated IFS newline-tab line dropped;
- the ban on [ ] in bash removed (dialect decides);
- the empty-array idiom becomes ${a[@]+"${a[@]}"}, because the plain form fails on 3.2/4.0/4.2 under set -u;
- -S warning removed.

12. Hypothesis verdicts:
- H1 refuted;
- H2 split (suppression, not absence);
- H3 confirmed and sharpened (pwsh curly quotes, shared POSIX quoter fails 17-18/20);
- H4 refuted for installers;
- H5 confirmed and extended;
- H7 confirmed (read only);
- H8 confirmed;
- H9 split (nu churns most, but ocx's guarded nu passes the floor).

